(MOJO-V EXO LIBRARY: PURPOSE, DESIGN, WORKFLOW, AND LLVM PORT TRADE-OFFS) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1\) WHAT THE EXO LIBRARY IS) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The **Mojo-V EXO library** is a C/C++ header-based compatibility layer that exposes encrypted) Tj
T*
(integer and floating-point programming abstractions to software today, on top of existing) Tj
T*
(compilers, while targeting the Mojo-V execution model.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(At a code level, EXO is centered on:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `exo/mojov-exo.h`: C++ encrypted scalar wrappers \(`inte_t<Bits, Signed>`, `fpe_t<Bits>`\) and) Tj
T*
(overloads for arithmetic, bitwise, relational, conversion, and `cmov` operations.) Tj
T*
(- `exo/mojov-intrinsics.h`: low-level inline-assembly intrinsics \(`_add`, `_mul`, `_fadd`,) Tj
T*
(`_slt`, `_cmov`, etc.\) that map EXO operations onto Mojo-V instruction semantics.) Tj
T*
(- Storage-type indirection \(`EXO_UINT64E_STORAGE_TYPE`, `EXO_FP64E_STORAGE_TYPE`\) allowing a) Tj
T*
(build to choose fast, strong, or proof-carrying encrypted memory payload types.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This design gives developers an encrypted-type programming model before a complete LLVM) Tj
T*
(language+backend integration exists.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2\) WHAT EXO IS USED FOR) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(EXO is used to:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. **Write encrypted algorithms in ordinary C++ syntax**) Tj
T*
(   - Example benchmarks include bubble sort, GEMM, knapsack, PSI, NTT kernel, etc., each) Tj
T*
(including `mojov-exo.h` and instantiating EXO encrypted types.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. **Exercise Mojo-V semantics in bring-up and evaluation**) Tj
T*
(   - The Mojo-V type tests \(`bringup-bench/mojov-typetests`\) validate arithmetic, comparisons,) Tj
T*
(assignment variants, casts, and conditional moves over EXO types.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. **Support multiple protection formats from the same source code**) Tj
T*
(   - By defining storage macros before including EXO, benchmark builds can target fast or) Tj
T*
(strong memory-encryption layouts without rewriting algorithm code.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. **Enable debug-time plaintext checks in simulation**) Tj
T*
(   - EXO provides `debug_context\(...\)` and `.decrypt\(\)` support \(for test/debug\) that decrypt) Tj
T*
(values using SIMON key expansion and a contract signature.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3\) HOW EXO WORKS \(MECHANICS\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A. TYPE LAYER AND OPERATOR OVERLOADING) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(EXO introduces encrypted scalar classes:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `inte_t<Bits, IsSigned>` for encrypted integers) Tj
T*
(- `fpe_t<Bits>` for encrypted floating point \(32/64 aliases\)) Tj
ET
