() Tj
T*
(These classes:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Store encrypted payloads \(not plaintext\) using selected storage structs.) Tj
T*
(- Overload arithmetic/logic/comparison operators to preserve C++ ergonomics.) Tj
T*
(- Return encrypted predicates \(rather than plaintext bools\), keeping control decisions) Tj
T*
(expressible via data-oblivious mechanisms.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(B. INTRINSIC MAPPING THROUGH INLINE ASSEMBLY) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Each EXO operator funnels into intrinsics from `mojov-intrinsics.h`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Examples:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `a + b` -> `_add\(...\)`) Tj
T*
(- `a < b` \(unsigned\) -> `_sltu\(...\)`) Tj
T*
(- `fp_a + fp_b` -> `_fadd\(...\)`) Tj
T*
(- `cmov\(pred, t, f\)` -> `_cmov\(...\)` / `_fcmov\(...\)`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The intrinsics load encrypted operands, execute arithmetic/relational instructions, and store) Tj
T*
(encrypted results. Logical operators are explicitly implemented without short-circuit behavior) Tj
T*
(to maintain data-oblivious semantics.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(C. EXPLICIT DATA-OBLIVIOUS SELECTION MODEL) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Instead of relying on plaintext branches over secret data, EXO provides `cmov\(...\)` overloads) Tj
T*
(for integer and floating-point cases, enabling branchless secret-dependent selection patterns) Tj
T*
(compatible with Mojo-V expectations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(D. CONFIGURABLE ENCRYPTED MEMORY ABI) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(By setting:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `EXO_UINT64E_STORAGE_TYPE`) Tj
T*
(- `EXO_FP64E_STORAGE_TYPE`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(before including `mojov-exo.h`, the same C++ source can bind to:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- `mojov_mem_fast_*`) Tj
T*
(- `mojov_mem_strong_*`) Tj
T*
(- `mojov_mem_proofcarrying_*`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This decouples algorithm code from encryption-format representation details.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(E. DEBUG DECRYPTION PATH FOR VERIFICATION \(NON-PRODUCTION SEMANTIC AID\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
